what_i_learned: |
  Today was focused on sharing progress and learning from others. My team presented our weekly update, where we discussed the work we completed throughout the week, including exploring datasets, refining our project direction, and making progress on our design document. Presenting our work helped me practice explaining our project clearly and confidently.

  One of the most interesting parts of the day was listening to presentations from other groups. It was exciting to see the variety of projects being worked on throughout the program. Each team was studying a different topic, which exposed me to new ideas and areas of research that I had not thought about before.

  By watching the other presentations, I learned that there are many different ways to approach a problem. Seeing how other teams organized their work and explained their ideas gave me new perspectives that may be helpful for our own project.

  The presentations also showed the value of teamwork and learning from others. Hearing about different experiences and approaches helped broaden my understanding of the work being done across the program.

blockers: |
  I did not encounter any major blockers today. The main challenge was making sure our presentation clearly communicated our progress while staying within the time limit.

reflection: |
  Today was enjoyable because it gave me the opportunity to see what everyone else in the program has been working on. While I spend most of my time focused on my own project, it was interesting to learn about the different topics and ideas being explored by other teams.

  Presenting our weekly update also allowed me to reflect on how much progress our team has made over the past week. It felt rewarding to share our accomplishments and see how our project has developed.

  Overall, today was both informative and inspiring. I enjoyed learning about other projects, improving my presentation skills, and gaining a greater appreciation for the variety of work taking place throughout the program.
